{"timestamp":"2026-07-22T11:19:28.923Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","call_id":"call_cGMEZQfY92ctTzBaS5raryaz","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:5:Rational Numbers in K\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:9:quotient between two integers. The sort representing these values is `Rat`.\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:10:`Int` is a subsort of `Rat`, and it is guaranteed that any integer will be\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:19:  syntax Rat\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:21:  syntax Rat ::= Int\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:34:  syntax Rat ::= left:\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:35:                 Rat \"^Rat\" Int [function, total, symbol(_^Rat_),  smtlib(ratpow), hook(RAT.pow)]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:37:                 Rat \"*Rat\" Rat [function, total, symbol(_*Rat_),  left, smtlib(ratmul), hook(RAT.mul)]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:38:               | Rat \"/Rat\" Rat [function,             symbol(_/Rat_),  left, smtlib(ratdiv), hook(RAT.div)]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:40:                 Rat \"+Rat\" Rat [function, total, symbol(_+Rat_),  left, smtlib(ratadd), hook(RAT.add)]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:41:               | Rat \"-Rat\" Rat [function, total, symbol(_-Rat_),  left, smtlib(ratsub), hook(RAT.sub)]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:52:  syntax Bool ::= Rat  \"==Rat\" Rat [function, total, symbol(_==Rat_),  smtlib(rateq), hook(RAT.eq)]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:53:                | Rat \"=/=Rat\" Rat [function, total, symbol(_=/=Rat_), smtlib(ratne), hook(RAT.ne)]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:54:                | Rat   \">Rat\" Rat [function, total, symbol(_>Rat_),   smtlib(ratgt), hook(RAT.gt)]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:55:                | Rat  \">=Rat\" Rat [function, total, symbol(_>=Rat_),  smtlib(ratge), hook(RAT.ge)]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:56:                | Rat   \"<Rat\" Rat [function, total, symbol(_<Rat_),   smtlib(ratlt), hook(RAT.lt)]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:57:                | Rat  \"<=Rat\" Rat [function, total, symbol(_<=Rat_),  smtlib(ratle), hook(RAT.le)]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:66:  syntax Rat ::= minRat(Rat, Rat) [function, total, symbol(minRat), smtlib(ratmin), hook(RAT.min)]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:67:               | maxRat(Rat, Rat) [function, total, symbol(maxRat), smtlib(ratmax), hook(RAT.max)]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:70:Conversion to Floating Point\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:74:is representable in a `Float` of a specified number of precision and exponent\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:78:  syntax Float ::= Rat2Float(Rat, precision: Int, exponentBits: Int) [function]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:82:Implementation of Rational Numbers\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:92:`I /Rat J` such that\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:99:  // invariant of < I , J >Rat : I =/= 0, J >= 2, and I and J are coprime\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:100:  syntax Rat ::= \"<\" Int \",\" Int \">Rat\" [format(%2 /Rat %4)]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:109:    #Ceil(@R1:Rat /Rat @R2:Rat)\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:111:    {(@R2 =/=Rat 0) #Equals true} #And #Ceil(@R1) #And #Ceil(@R2)\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:125:  rule R ==Rat S => R ==K S\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:127:  rule R =/=Rat S => R =/=K S\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:142:  rule < I , I' >Rat +Rat < J , J' >Rat => ((I *Int J') +Int (I' *Int J)) /Rat (I' *Int J')\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:143:  rule I:Int         +Rat < J , J' >Rat => ((I *Int J') +Int J) /Rat J'\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:144:  rule < J , J' >Rat +Rat I:Int         => I +Rat < J , J' >Rat\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:145:  rule I:Int         +Rat J:Int         => I +Int J\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:147:  rule < I , I' >Rat *Rat < J , J' >Rat => (I *Int J) /Rat (I' *Int J')\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:148:  rule I:Int         *Rat < J , J' >Rat => (I *Int J) /Rat J'\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:149:  rule < J , J' >Rat *Rat I:Int         => I *Rat < J , J' >Rat\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:150:  rule I:Int         *Rat J:Int         => I *Int J\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:152:  rule < I , I' >Rat /Rat < J , J' >Rat => (I *Int J') /Rat (I' *Int J)\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:153:  rule I:Int         /Rat < J , J' >Rat => (I *Int J') /Rat J\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:154:  rule < I , I' >Rat /Rat J:Int         => I /Rat (I' *Int J) requires J =/=Int 0\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:155:  rule I:Int         /Rat J:Int         => makeRat(I, J)      requires J =/=Int 0\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:159:  rule R -Rat S => R +Rat (-1 *Rat S)\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:163:  syntax Rat ::= makeRat(Int, Int)      [function]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:164:               | makeRat(Int, Int, Int) [function]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:166:  rule makeRat(0, J) => 0 requires J =/=Int 0\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:168:  rule makeRat(I, J) => makeRat(I, J, gcdInt(I,J)) requires I =/=Int 0 andBool J =/=Int 0\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:170:  // makeRat(I, J, D) is defined when I =/= 0, J =/= 0, D > 0, and D = gcd(I,J)\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:171:  rule makeRat(I, J, D) => I /Int D                       requires J ==Int D // implies J > 0 since D > 0\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:172:  rule makeRat(I, J, D) => < I /Int D , J /Int D >Rat     requires J >Int 0 andBool J =/=Int D\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:173:  rule makeRat(I, J, D) => makeRat(0 -Int I, 0 -Int J, D) requires J <Int 0\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:186:  rule _ ^Rat 0 => 1\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:187:  rule 0 ^Rat N => 0 requires N =/=Int 0\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:189:  rule < I , J >Rat ^Rat N => powRat(< I , J >Rat, N) requires N >Int 0\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:190:  rule X:Int        ^Rat N => X ^Int N                requires N >Int 0\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:192:  rule X ^Rat N => (1 /Rat X) ^Rat (0 -Int N) requires X =/=Rat 0 andBool N <Int 0\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:196:  syntax Rat ::= powRat(Rat, Int) [function]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:198:  // powRat(X, N) is defined when X =/= 0 and N > 0\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:199:  rule powRat(X, 1) => X\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:200:  rule powRat(X, N) => powRat(X *Rat X, N /Int 2) requires N >Int 1 andBool N %Int 2  ==Int 0\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:201:  rule powRat(X, N) => powRat(X, N -Int 1) *Rat X requires N >Int 1 andBool N %Int 2 =/=Int 0\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:207:  rule R >Rat S => R -Rat S >Rat 0 requires S =/=Rat 0\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:209:  rule < I , _ >Rat >Rat 0 => I >Int 0\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:210:  rule I:Int        >Rat 0 => I >Int 0\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:214:  rule R >=Rat S => notBool R <Rat S\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:216:  rule R <Rat S => S >Rat R\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:218:  rule R <=Rat S => S >=Rat R\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:220:  rule minRat(R, S) => R requires R <=Rat S\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:221:  rule minRat(R, S) => S requires S <=Rat R\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:223:  rule maxRat(R, S) => R requires R >=Rat S\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:224:  rule maxRat(R, S) => S requires S >=Rat R\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:226:  syntax Float ::= #Rat2Float(Int, Int, Int, Int) [function, hook(FLOAT.rat2float)]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:227:  rule Rat2Float(Num:Int, Prec:Int, Exp:Int) => #Rat2Float(Num, 1, Prec, Exp)\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/rat.md:228:  rule Rat2Float(< Num, Dem >Rat, Prec, Exp) => #Rat2Float(Num, Dem, Prec, Exp)\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1461:IEEE 754 Floating-point Numbers\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1494:  syntax Float [hook(FLOAT.Float)]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1495:  syntax Float ::= r\"([\\\\+\\\\-]?[0-9]+(\\\\.[0-9]*)?|\\\\.[0-9]+)([eE][\\\\+\\\\-]?[0-9]+)?([fFdD]|([pP][0-9]+[xX][0-9]+))?\" [token, prec(1)]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1496:  syntax Float ::= r\"[\\\\+\\\\-]?Infinity([fFdD]|([pP][0-9]+[xX][0-9]+))?\" [token, prec(3)]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1497:  syntax Float ::= r\"NaN([fFdD]|([pP][0-9]+[xX][0-9]+))?\" [token, prec(3)]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1506:### Float precision\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1508:You can retrieve the number of bits of precision in a `Float`.\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1511:  syntax Int ::= precisionFloat(Float) [function, total, hook(FLOAT.precision)]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1514:### Float exponent bits\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1516:You can retrieve the number of bits of exponent range in a `Float`.\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1519:  syntax Int ::= exponentBitsFloat(Float) [function, total, hook(FLOAT.exponentBits)]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1522:### Float exponent\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1524:You can retrieve the value of the exponent bits of a `Float` as an integer.\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1527:  syntax Int ::= exponentFloat(Float) [function, total, hook(FLOAT.exponent)]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1530:### Float sign\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1532:You can retrieve the value of the sign bit of a `Float` as a boolean. True\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1536:  syntax Bool ::= signFloat(Float)      [function, total, hook(FLOAT.sign)]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1539:### Float special values\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1541:You can check whether a `Float` value is infinite or Not-a-Number.\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1544:  syntax Bool ::= isNaN(Float)          [function, total, smt-hook(fp.isNaN), hook(FLOAT.isNaN)]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1545:                | isInfinite(Float)     [function, total]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1548:### Float arithmetic\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1552:* Compute the unary negation `--Float` of a float. `--Float X` is distinct\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1553:  from `0.0 -Float X`. For example, `0.0 -Float 0.0` is positive zero.\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1554:  `--Float 0.0` is negative zero.\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1555:* Compute the exponentation `^Float` of two floats.\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1556:* Compute the product `*Float`, quotient `/Float`, or remainder `%Float` of two\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1559:* Compute the sum `+Float` or difference `-Float` of two floats.\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1562:  syntax Float ::= \"--Float\" Float             [function, total, smt-hook(fp.neg), hook(FLOAT.neg)]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1563:                 > Float \"^Float\" Float        [function, left, hook(FLOAT.pow)]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1565:                   Float \"*Float\" Float        [function, left, smt-hook((fp.mul roundNearestTiesToEven #1 #2)), hook(FLOAT.mul)]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1566:                 | Float \"/Float\" Float        [function, left, smt-hook((fp.div roundNearestTiesToEven #1 #2)), hook(FLOAT.div)]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1567:                 | Float \"%Float\" Float        [function, left, smt-hook((fp.rem roundNearestTiesToEven #1 #2)), hook(FLOAT.rem)]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1569:                   Float \"+Float\" Float        [function, left, smt-hook((fp.add roundNearestTiesToEven #1 #2)), hook(FLOAT.add)]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1570:                 | Float \"-Float\" Float        [function, left, smt-hook((fp.sub roundNearestTiesToEven #1 #2)), hook(FLOAT.sub)]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1573:### Floating-point mathematics\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1577:* Compute the Nth integer root `rootFloat` of a float.\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1578:* Compute the absolute value `absFloat` of a float.\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1580:  range (`roundFloat`). The resulting `Float` will yield the specified values\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1581:  when calling `precisionFloat` and `exponentBitsFloat` and when performing\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1584:  (`floorFloat`).\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1586:  (`ceilFloat`).\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1588:  the direction of zero (`truncFloat`).\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1589:* Compute the natural exponential `expFloat` of a float (i.e. e^x).\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1590:* Compute the natural logarithm `logFloat` of a float.\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1591:* Compute the sine `sinFloat` of a float.\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1592:* Compute the cosine `cosFloat` of a float.\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1594:* Compute the arcsine `asinFloat` of a float.\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1595:* Compute the arccosine `acosFloat` of a float.\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1596:* Compute the arctangent `atanFloat` of a float.\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1597:* Compute the arctangent `atan2Float` of two floats.\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1598:* Compute the maximum `maxFloat` of two floats.\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1599:* Compute the minimum `minFloat` of two floats.\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1600:* Compute the square root `sqrtFloat` of a float.\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1602:  exponent range (`maxValueFloat`).\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1604:  precision and exponent range (`minValueFloat`).\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1607:  syntax Float ::= rootFloat(Float, Int)        [function, hook(FLOAT.root)]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1608:                 | absFloat(Float)              [function, total, smt-hook(fp.abs), hook(FLOAT.abs)]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1609:                 | roundFloat(Float, precision: Int, exponentBits: Int)  [function, hook(FLOAT.round)]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1610:                 | floorFloat(Float)            [function, total, hook(FLOAT.floor)]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1611:                 | ceilFloat(Float)             [function, total, hook(FLOAT.ceil)]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1612:                 | truncFloat(Float)            [function, total, hook(FLOAT.trunc)]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1613:                 | expFloat(Float)              [function, total, hook(FLOAT.exp)]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1614:                 | logFloat(Float)              [function, hook(FLOAT.log)]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1615:                 | sinFloat(Float)              [function, total, hook(FLOAT.sin)]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/domains.md:1616:                 | cosFloat(Float)              [function, total, hook(FLOAT.cos)]\n/usr/include/kframework/builtin/